From: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.com>
Date: Thu, 08 May 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] HACK: arm: compressed: sun5i AHB/MBUS settle after self-relocation copy

On Allwinner sun5i (R8/A13, C.H.I.P.) the zImage must self-relocate
when loaded to an address overlapping the final decompressed kernel
image. The backward ldmdb/stmdb copy loop writes ~1.5 MiB of zImage
data to a new DRAM address.

After the copy, cache_clean_flush() is called. With write-through
D-cache enabled (patch 0008, __arm926ejs_mmu_cache_on), the copy
stores went directly to DRAM as individual AHB/MBUS write transactions
-- no dirty D-cache lines to flush. cache_clean_flush() therefore
only invalidates I-cache and issues a DSB. DSB drains the CPU write
buffer but does NOT drain the MBUS arbiter's pending write transaction
queue.

After cache_clean_flush() returns:
  badr r0, restart       (PC-relative arithmetic -- no DRAM access)
  add  r0, r0, r6        (register arithmetic -- no DRAM access)
  mov  pc, r0            (branch to new DRAM location)

The 'mov pc, r0' causes an I-cache miss (I-cache just invalidated).
The fill goes IBUS -> AHB -> MBUS -> new DRAM location. MBUS has
~375,000 pending write transactions for that address range from the
1.5 MiB copy. The read stalls the CPU indefinitely.

Symptom: no 'D' UART marker (patch 0009), no earlycon, complete silence
after "[BOOT-DBG] sun5i: pre-kernel settle".

Fix: after 'bl cache_clean_flush' and before 'badr r0, restart',
insert a DSB + busy-wait settle. The settle instructions are fetched
from the OLD (source) location -- no pending MBUS writes there -- so
fetches succeed and the tight loop runs from I-cache while MBUS drains.
By the time 'mov pc, r0' executes, MBUS is idle.

Settle: 0x04000000 = 67,108,864 iters * ~3 cycles/iter @ 1 GHz = 200ms.
r0 is scratch after cache_clean_flush returns; r6 (reloc offset) is
preserved across the settle.

Guarded by #ifdef CONFIG_MACH_SUN5I.

Signed-off-by: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S
@@ -533,6 +533,24 @@
 		mov	r0, r9			@ start of relocated zImage
 		add	r1, sp, r6		@ end of relocated zImage
 		bl	cache_clean_flush
+#ifdef CONFIG_MACH_SUN5I
+		/*
+		 * sun5i AHB/MBUS: settle after self-relocation write burst.
+		 * ~1.5 MiB of zImage data was copied to a new DRAM address.
+		 * MBUS retains those write transactions; the first instruction
+		 * fetch at the new 'restart' address (I-cache miss after
+		 * cache_clean_flush invalidated I-cache) stalls indefinitely.
+		 * Settle runs from OLD location (copy source) -- no pending
+		 * writes there, so fetches succeed and the loop runs from
+		 * I-cache while MBUS drains the ~1.5 MiB write backlog.
+		 * r0 is scratch after cache_clean_flush; r6 preserved.
+		 */
+		mcr	p15, 0, r0, c7, c10, 4		@ DSB
+		mov	r0, #0x04000000			@ ~200ms @ 1GHz
+sun5i_reloc_settle:
+		subs	r0, r0, #1
+		bne	sun5i_reloc_settle
+#endif

 		badr	r0, restart
 		add	r0, r0, r6
